# Parquet is internally compressed, so git cannot delta successive versions —
# every ETL run stores 10-25 MB of fresh whole blobs. Tracking the tables in LFS
# keeps that churn out of the pack. Existing blobs stay in history; this only
# stops the growth.
#
# CI must fetch them: .github/workflows/pages.yml sets `lfs: true` on checkout,
# because actions/checkout does NOT pull LFS objects by default. Without it the
# build sees pointer files and Store() fails (with the message it raises for
# exactly this case).
data/parquet/*.parquet filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
